<title>BELGIUM: EU to assess GATT sugar export limit.</title>
<headline>EU to assess GATT sugar export limit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's sugar management committee will on Wednesday review the amount of sugar available for export with respect to the GATT (General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade) ceiling, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Under the new regulation introduced on July 1 last year the Commmission has the power to reduce quotas, even in the current marketing year, if the GATT limit means that sugar cannot be exported and if it cannot, alternatively, be stored,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Currently the Commission believes that the amount available for export in 1996/97 will not breach the GATT limit.</p>
<p>&quot;The exercise on Wednesday will have no real impact. The review is being undertaken to ensure that the proceedures are in place should the need to cut quotas ever arise,&quot; a European Commission official added.</p>
</text>
